course: dictionary
lesson: 9978
title: Teardrop: a tear or a shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. A teardrop is a single tear that falls from the eye. A teardrop is also a shape: round at the bottom and pointed at the top.
explain: «Small raindrops are round, and bigger ones are flattened at the bottom like a burger bun as they fall; none is shaped like a teardrop.» The words «round», «flattened» and «shaped» are clues. They are talking about shapes, so teardrop here means the shape, not a tear.
explain: «For the fun myths, look closely: raindrops aren't teardrop-shaped» The ending «-shaped» is a clue: it means having a certain shape. Check by swapping in the meaning: «raindrops aren't round at the bottom and pointed at the top» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: A teardrop is a single tear falling from the eye.
fact: A teardrop shape is round at the bottom and pointed at the top, like a falling drop of water.
fact: «Teardrop-shaped» means having the shape of a teardrop.
fact: Real raindrops are not teardrop-shaped: «Small raindrops are round», and bigger ones are flattened at the bottom.
fact: Useful phrases: a single teardrop, teardrop shape, teardrop earrings.
exercise: In «none is shaped like a teardrop», what does teardrop mean? | A single tear from the eye | *A shape that is round at the bottom and pointed at the top | A burger bun | A big, flat raindrop
exercise: Which word in «raindrops aren't teardrop-shaped» is the clue that teardrop describes a shape? | raindrops | *shaped | aren't | myths
exercise: Which of these means a tear falling from the eye? | a burger bun | heat lightning | *a single teardrop | a teardrop shape
test: What does «teardrop-shaped» mean? | *Having the shape of a teardrop: round at the bottom, pointed at the top | A tear running down a cheek | Flat and wide like a bun | Falling quickly from the sky
test: Which shape is a teardrop? | *A drop that is round at the bottom and pointed at the top | A flat, wide bun | A square with four equal sides | A perfect circle
exam: Read «raindrops aren't teardrop-shaped» and choose the meaning of teardrop here. | *A shape: round at the bottom and pointed at the top | A type of bread | A tear falling from the eye | A flash of heat lightning
